  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Genesis",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 44,
    "summary": "Joseph arranges to stop the return of his brothers to Canaan—Judah offers himself in place of Benjamin for their father’s sake.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And he commanded the steward of his house, saying, Fill the men’s sacks with food, as much as they can carry, and put every man’s money in his sack’s mouth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 76
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:1",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And put my cup, the silver cup, in the sack’s mouth of the youngest, and his corn money. And he did according to the word that Joseph had spoken.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:2",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "As soon as the morning was light, the men were sent away, they and their asses.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:3",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And when they were gone out of the city, and not yet far off, Joseph said unto his steward, Up, follow after the men; and when thou dost overtake them, say unto them, Wherefore have ye rewarded evil for good?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 44
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:4",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Is not this it in which my lord drinketh, and whereby indeed he divineth? ye have done evil in so doing.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 14
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:5",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And he overtook them, and he spake unto them these same words.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:6",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And they said unto him, Wherefore saith my lord these words? God forbid that thy servants should do according to this thing:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:7",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, the money, which we found in our sacks’ mouths, we brought again unto thee out of the land of Canaan: how then should we steal out of thy lord’s house silver or gold?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:8",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "With whomsoever of thy servants it be found, both let him die, and we also will be my lord’s bondmen.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:9",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And he said, Now also let it be according unto your words: he with whom it is found shall be my servant; and ye shall be blameless.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 25
          },
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 31
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:10",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Then they speedily took down every man his sack to the ground, and opened every man his sack.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:11",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And he searched, and began at the eldest, and left at the youngest: and the cup was found in Benjamin’s sack.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 20
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:12",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Then they rent their clothes, and laded every man his ass, and returned to the city.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 14,
            "text": "Job 1:20; Eccl. 3:7; Alma 46:12 (12–23)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:13",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And Judah and his brethren came to Joseph’s house; for he was yet there: and they fell before him on the ground.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "Gen. 37:7 (7, 9–10); 42:6; 43:26 (26–28)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:14",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And Joseph said unto them, What deed is this that ye have done? wot ye not that such a man as I can certainly divine?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 39
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:15",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And Judah said, What shall we say unto my lord? what shall we speak? or how shall we clear ourselves? God hath found out the iniquity of thy servants: behold, we are my lord’s servants, both we, and he also with whom the cup is found.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 162,
            "end": 165
          },
          {
            "start": 199,
            "end": 201
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:16",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And he said, God forbid that I should do so: but the man in whose hand the cup is found, he shall be my servant; and as for you, get you up in peace unto your father.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 44:17",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 44,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Judah came near unto him, and said, Oh my lord, let thy servant, I pray thee, speak a word in my lord’s ears, and let not thine anger burn against thy servant: for thou art even as Pharaoh.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "Gen. 43:20."
          },
          {
            "start": 133,
            "end": 138,
            "text": "Ex. 32:22."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 174,
            "end": 177
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [
